repository-code: "https://github.com/marcobornstein/SWIFT"
license: MIT
version: 2.0.1
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of SWIFT, a wait-free decentralized federated
  learning algorithm in which clients never block on one another: each
  broadcasts its model to its neighbours and averages in whatever has arrived.
  SWIFT is the first asynchronous decentralized federated learning algorithm to
  obtain the optimal O(1/sqrt(T)) convergence rate without a bounded-delay
  assumption; in the paper's experiments it reduces communication time by
  nearly an order of magnitude and run time by upwards of 50% against
  synchronous baselines. Includes the D-SGD, PA-SGD and LD-SGD baselines, one
  configuration per experiment in the paper, and tooling to reproduce its
  tables and figures.
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - decentralized optimization
  - asynchronous SGD
  - distributed machine learning
  - MPI
  - PyTorch
